        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/a02zo9qeklrv5u9j55cy7ft5a">

          
    
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-09-10T09:25:11.220Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_wtfnow-energytransition-leadership-activity-7503745379369316353-hq8F","text":"Looking back at our past season of WTF now, this clip stuck with us.\n\nBloombergNEF founder Michael Liebreich has a simple rule: whenever you see the phrase \"primary energy\", in reports, boardroom decks, policy documents, ask yourself whether the author or commentator actually know what it means, or are they counting on the fact that you don't?\n\nIn today's energy system, two-thirds of primary energy is wasted before it does anything useful. An electrified system based on renewables can deliver 2–3x the end-use efficiency.\n\nThe shift is already happening. But most consumers are unaware and most boardrooms are are still planning like it isn't.\n\n🎧 Full episode on Spotify and Apple Podcasts\n▶️ Watch on YouTube: https://lnkd.in/eHxi_5bm\n\n#WTFNow #EnergyTransition #Leadership #Sustainability #ClimateAction","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_wtfnow-energytransition-leadership-activity-7503745379369316353-hq8F"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-09-04T11:27:02.054Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_ceos-corporateculture-businessleadership-activity-7501601715754811392-xhPp","text":"CEOs instinctively polish the story for external audiences before it's even settled internally — and in doing so, drain it of the honesty that makes people trust it.\n\nBut in a transformation, building a narrative isn't just about communicating the final product. It's a tool for building shared understanding through co-authorship — about why change is necessary, what it means for people, and where the organisation is actually headed.\n\nIn our experience, it's best to protect that narrative from too much polish. Front it early, even when you're still unsure. Being seen working it out is what builds alignment.\n\n#CEOs #CorporateCulture #BusinessLeadership #FutureOfWork #Strategy","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_ceos-corporateculture-businessleadership-activity-7501601715754811392-xhPp"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-08-27T14:06:37.747Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_strategy-leadership-executiveteams-activity-7498742776323358720-12Dz","text":"At S7, we often come across leadership teams that are not aligned on what they believe about what their industry and macro context will look like over the medium term.\n\nBut without a set of shared 'strategic beliefs', they struggle to make or explain strategic choices.\n\nIn our experience, when strategy discussions keeps looping, it's often because the team hasn't agreed what they believe about the future and therefore can't describe what company they want to lead in light of that future. Surface the beliefs and the choices resolve.\n\n#Strategy #Leadership #ExecutiveTeams #StrategicPlanning #OrganizationalAlignment","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_strategy-leadership-executiveteams-activity-7498742776323358720-12Dz"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-08-19T06:57:02.342Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-transformation-chro-activity-7495735563518640128-GMLH","text":"Transformation shouldn't feel like homework.\n\nBut that's exactly what happens in a lot of organisations: leaders are asked to bolt \"academic\" change work onto their existing responsibilities instead of programmes being useful in their everyday work.\n\nThe result? Change feels like a burden, rather than an empowering and exciting opportunity.\n\nOver the years, we've learned that for transformation to work, it needs to feel integral to the day-to-day.\n\n#Leadership #Transformation #CHRO #OrganisationalChange #PeopleStrategy","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-transformation-chro-activity-7495735563518640128-GMLH"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-08-13T09:45:41.000Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_weve-spent-decades-helping-executive-teams-activity-7493603676985401344-vzJW","text":"We've spent decades helping executive teams mobilise their leaders in service of transformation. Along the way, we've learned a thing or two about what works and - crucially - what doesn't. \n\nMost transformations fail. And, when they do, it's almost always for one or more of six reasons.\n\nSound familiar? If this resonates or speaks to something you need help solving for, we'd love to hear from you.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_weve-spent-decades-helping-executive-teams-activity-7493603676985401344-vzJW"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-08-05T14:15:01.215Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-geopolitics-strategy-activity-7490772354953003008-4egS","text":"\"The guilt lies with them. The blame lies with us.\"\n\nLooking back at Season 2 of WTF Now?, this section from our very first episode still holds up.\n\nWith tensions rising around the world and global institutions under pressure, Graeme Lamb's warning from our season opener is worth another listen. Are we at risk of repeating mistakes from the past through silence and appeasement?\n\nGraeme says business leaders need to \"wake up and smell the coffee\" arguing how important it is to call out bad behaviour and hold elected officials to higher standards. Because if not, we might wake up in something akin to 1939.\n\n🎧 Listen to the full episode here: https://lnkd.in/eqtczAU4\n📺 Watch on YouTube: https://lnkd.in/ekayqkGN\n\nOne of several Season 2 moments we're looking back on this summer. Season 3 is on its way.\n\n#Leadership #Geopolitics #Strategy #GlobalAffairs #HistoryMatters #FutureOfBusiness","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-geopolitics-strategy-activity-7490772354953003008-4egS"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-07-17T08:03:43.427Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_climate-nationalsecurity-climaterisk-activity-7483793545695469568-h69j","text":"With another heatwave moving across Europe, this conversation from Season 2 feels worth revisiting.\n\nIn this clip from our podcast WTF Now?, Erin Sikorsky highlights a growing but often overlooked consequence of climate change:\n\n🔥 Militaries around the world are being deployed more frequently to respond to extreme weather: fires, floods, storms. Leaving less time and capacity to prepare for traditional security challenges.\n\n🌍 As these deployments become more frequent and more intense, leaders in many capitals are beginning to ask a difficult question: Is this sustainable?\n\nThis isn't a future scenario. It's already reshaping military readiness, strategic planning, and risk assumptions.\n\n🎧 Watch the full conversation with Erin Sikorsky on WTF Now? here: https://lnkd.in/eppuJZdB\n\nOne of several Season 2 moments we're looking back on this summer. Season 3 is on its way.\n\n#Climate #NationalSecurity #ClimateRisk #ClimateChange #Resilience #StrategicRisk #Geopolitics #WTFNowPodcast Rick Wheatley","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_climate-nationalsecurity-climaterisk-activity-7483793545695469568-h69j"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-07-02T09:57:15.506Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-militaryleadership-wtfnow-activity-7478386299683659776-fc-V","text":"Before crossing into Iraq in 1991, now retired three-star US Army general and former Commanding General of US Army Europe Mark Hertling, DBA started writing lessons to his two young sons, in case he didn't come home.\n\nWhen his son found and typed up the journal decades later, it became the outline for his book, \"If I Don't Return\".\n\nIn the season finale of WTF Now?, Mark joins S7 - Systems7's Rick Wheatley to talk about the book, what's really happening to America, and what it takes to lead large organisations through turbulent times — the kind of honest, clear-eyed perspective that feels increasingly rare right now. From someone who has done it where the stakes were literally life and death.\n\n🎧 Watch the full episode here: https://lnkd.in/e99NWZxd\n\n🔔 This episode wraps up Season 2, thanks for tuning in. Subscribe now so you don't miss Season 3 in the fall!\n\n#Leadership #MilitaryLeadership #WTFNow #IfIDontReturn #Fatherhood #AmericaWillBeBack #Podcast","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-militaryleadership-wtfnow-activity-7478386299683659776-fc-V"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-07-01T10:30:13.861Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_culture-leadership-transformation-activity-7478032209560498177-DXWs","text":"They had values on the wall, on the screensavers, in the onboarding packs, in the annual report.\n\nWhat they didn't have was leaders who could tell you — in their own words, without looking at a slide — what those values actually meant for how they ran their teams.\n\nCulture doesn't live in documents. It lives in daily decisions, in the conversations leaders choose to have... and avoid.\n\nWe worked with their leadership community to make the values real. Not as a communications exercise - as a leadership one.\n\nThe question we kept coming back to was: what would have to change about how you lead, for these values to actually be true here?\n\nThat's an uncomfortable question, but it's also the only one worth asking.\n\n#Culture #Leadership #Transformation #S7 #OrganisationalChange\n","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_culture-leadership-transformation-activity-7478032209560498177-DXWs"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7"},"datePublished":"2026-06-24T10:00:14.670Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-geopolitics-transformation-activity-7475487948151492608-pPHd","text":"Every leader has a map. A set of assumptions about how their market works, how their industry is structured, what good looks like.\n\nFor years, those maps were reliable enough. They're not anymore.\n\nGeopolitical shifts are redrawing supply chains overnight. The energy transition is restructuring entire industries. AI is changing the economics of almost everything. The assumptions that underpinned most long-term strategies five years ago are quietly becoming liabilities.\n\nThe problem isn't that leaders don't know the map has changed - most of them sense it. The problem is that organisations move at the speed of their leaders' collective understanding — and that understanding takes time to build.\n\nThe leaders who navigate disruption well aren't the ones with the best new map. They're the ones who've learned to lead without one.\n\nThat means building clarity in conditions of uncertainty and making decisions with incomplete information. Keeping teams moving when the destination keeps shifting.\n\nThat's not a strategic skill. It's a leadership one.\n\n#Leadership #Geopolitics #Transformation #Strategy #OrganisationalChange #S7 #WTFNow","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/systems7_leadership-geopolitics-transformation-activity-7475487948151492608-pPHd"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"S7 - Systems7","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/systems7","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Oslo","addressRegion":"Oslo","addressCountry":"NO"},"description":"Systems7 – S7 for short  – is an Oslo-based advisory firm that exists to help the businesses that matter to the future outperform the ones that don’t.\n\nToday we are a tight-knit group that loves working together, drawing on deep shared experiences from supporting senior leaders in some of the world's biggest, most well-known companies.\n\nThrough six modular offerings, we help leaders drive transformation in their teams and organisations – in line with the health of the environmental, social, political and geopolitical systems in which they operate.\n\nOffering 1: Developing leaders and teams to enable strategic and commercial aims.\nOffering 2: Equipping leadership teams for change.\nOffering 3: Building contextual fluency in order to enable decision-making against uncertainty.\nOffering 4: Aligning on your company´s strategic direction.\nOffering 5: Mobilising the wider organisation, so the people required for implementation understand and support your transformation. \nOffering 6: Accelerating impact performance and moving beyond ESG compliance to impact-driven value creation.\n+\nServices tailored for portfolio managers – from community-building events for portfolio leaders to 'impact sprints'  to help portfolio companies develop targets and KPIs to drive ESG performance.\n+\nInspiring experiences for your leaders and teams – from panels and workshops to large-scale conferences and adventurous field trips in the great outdoors. \n\nWant to know more? Get in touch: inquiries@systems7.co or visit our website www.systems7.co\n\nWe also host the podcast WTF? Now by S7 - for business leaders trying to make sense of a world that's stopped making sense. Check it out on podcast.s7.wtf","numberOfEmployees":{"value":13,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/C4D0BAQHV_BmuaTiyTg/company-logo_200_200/company-logo_200_200/0/1630579561564/systems7_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=faA0pwpX45NZ1oM1fV2TOHOzuj7mcRQqAivm5vYNIvE","description":"S7 - Systems7","@type":"ImageObject"},"slogan":"Helping the companies that matter to the future outperform the ones who don't. \nWe also host the podcast \"WTF Now by S7\"","sameAs":"http://www.systems7.co"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
