  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">CEOs instinctively polish the story for external audiences before it's even settled internally — and in doing so, drain it of the honesty that makes people trust it.

But in a transformation, building a narrative isn't just about communicating the final product. It's a tool for building shared understanding through co-authorship — about why change is necessary, what it means for people, and where the organisation is actually headed.

In our experience, it's best to protect that narrative from too much polish. Front it early, even when you're still unsure. Being seen working it out is what builds alignment.

