  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">At S7, we often come across leadership teams that are not aligned on what they believe about what their industry and macro context will look like over the medium term.

But without a set of shared 'strategic beliefs', they struggle to make or explain strategic choices.

In our experience, when strategy discussions keeps looping, it's often because the team hasn't agreed what they believe about the future and therefore can't describe what company they want to lead in light of that future. Surface the beliefs and the choices resolve.

